
---
const examples = [
  { dollars: "$100", rupees: "₹8,850", afterFees: "₹8,628.75" },
  { dollars: "$500", rupees: "₹44,250", afterFees: "₹43,143.75" },
  { dollars: "$1,000", rupees: "₹88,500", afterFees: "₹86,287.50" },
  { dollars: "$2,000", rupees: "₹177,000", afterFees: "₹172,575.00" },
];
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Convert US dollars to Indian rupees with our USD to INR calculator. Estimate currency conversion, payment processing fees and your final payout."
    />
    <title>USD to INR Calculator – Convert Dollars to Rupees | DollarDost</title>
  </head>

  <body>
    <header>
      <a href="/" class="logo">DollarDost<span>.</span></a>
      <a href="/#calculator" class="nav-link">Currency Calculator →</a>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="hero">
        <span class="eyebrow">FREE CURRENCY TOOL</span>

        <h1>USD to INR Calculator</h1>

        <p class="subtitle">
          Convert US dollars into Indian rupees and estimate how much money
          you'll receive after payment processing fees.
        </p>

        <a href="/#calculator" class="button">
          Calculate Your USD to INR Payout →
        </a>

        <p class="note">
          Use your own exchange rate and fees for a personalized estimate.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="content">
        <h2>How to convert USD to INR</h2>

        <p>
          Converting US dollars (USD) into Indian rupees (INR) is simple.
          Multiply the amount in dollars by the exchange rate to calculate
          its value in rupees.
        </p>

        <div class="formula">
          INR amount = USD amount × exchange rate
        </div>

        <p>
          For example, if the exchange rate is ₹88.50 for every US dollar,
          $100 is equivalent to ₹8,850 before any fees.
        </p>

        <h2>USD to INR conversion examples</h2>

        <p>
          The following examples use an illustrative exchange rate of
          ₹88.50 per USD and a hypothetical payment fee of 2.5%.
          Actual exchange rates and fees vary by provider.
        </p>

        <div class="table-wrapper">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>USD amount</th>
                <th>Before fees</th>
                <th>After 2.5% fee</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>

            <tbody>
              {examples.map((example) => (
                <tr>
                  <td>{example.dollars}</td>
                  <td>{example.rupees}</td>
                  <td>{example.afterFees}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h2>Why is my USD to INR payout different?</h2>

        <p>
          The amount you receive in your Indian bank account may differ
          from the amount shown using a currency exchange rate. Payment
          providers may charge transaction fees, currency conversion
          markups or additional fixed fees.
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Exchange rate:</strong> The rate your payment provider
            uses to convert USD into INR.
          </li>

          <li>
            <strong>Processing fee:</strong> A percentage deducted from
            your payment.
          </li>

          <li>
            <strong>Fixed fee:</strong> An additional flat charge that may
            apply to a transaction.
          </li>

          <li>
            <strong>Currency markup:</strong> A difference between the
            market exchange rate and the provider's offered rate.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Calculate your dollar payout in rupees</h2>

        <p>
          Whether you're a freelancer, remote worker, creator or business
          receiving international payments, knowing your estimated payout
          can help you understand what you'll actually receive.
        </p>

        <p>
          Enter your payment amount, exchange rate and fees into our
          calculator to estimate your take-home payout.
        </p>

        <a href="/#calculator" class="button">
          Open the USD to INR Calculator →
        </a>

        <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

        <details>
          <summary>How much is $100 in Indian rupees?</summary>
          <p>
            At an illustrative rate of ₹88.50 per USD, $100 equals ₹8,850
            before fees. The actual amount depends on the exchange rate
            offered by your payment provider.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>How much is $1,000 in INR?</summary>
          <p>
            At ₹88.50 per USD, $1,000 equals ₹88,500 before fees.
            If a 2.5% fee applies, the estimated payout is ₹86,287.50.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Does this calculator use live exchange rates?</summary>
          <p>
            No. The calculator uses a manually entered exchange rate.
            You can enter the rate quoted by your bank, payment provider
            or currency exchange service.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Why do international payment providers charge fees?</summary>
          <p>
            Providers may charge transaction fees for processing
            international payments and currency conversions. The fee
            structure varies by provider, payment method and transaction.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Can freelancers use this calculator?</summary>
          <p>
            Yes. Freelancers, remote workers, creators, consultants and
            businesses can use it to estimate international payment
            conversions and deductions.
          </p>
        </details>

        <div class="disclaimer">
          <strong>Disclaimer:</strong> Exchange rates shown in examples are
          illustrative and are not live market rates or financial advice.
          Actual payouts may vary depending on your provider's exchange
          rate, fees and other deductions.
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <a href="/" class="logo">DollarDost<span>.</span></a>
      <p>Your dost for dollar earnings.</p>
      <p>© 2026 DollarDost</p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  * {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

